      {
        "id": "capacity-energy-and-conclusion",
        "type": "text",
        "heading": "Capacity and environmental performance need separate evidence",
        "content": "Production capacity describes potential annual throughput under stated assumptions, while production describes material actually manufactured. USGS reports both for Iran, and also separates cement from clinker. Their figures answer different questions and should not be added together or treated as equivalent measures of demand. [s2]\n\nEnergy and emissions add another layer. Kiln heat is central to making clinker; grinding and handling are additional operations. Dust control addresses particulate emissions, while reducing carbon dioxide requires attention to fuel use and mineral chemistry. Process references explain these mechanisms, but they cannot prove the performance of an Iranian factory without local measurements. The industry's clearest assessment therefore combines correctly defined output with plant-level operating and environmental evidence. [s3][s5]",
        "source_ids": ["s2", "s3", "s5"]
      }
